# Branch-per-feature workflow

For every **new feature**, **refactor**, or **change**, create a new Git branch so that changes are kept separate and easier to review or revert.

- **Before starting work**: create and switch to a branch, e.g. `feature/short-name` or `fix/issue-name` or `refactor/area`.
- **After work is done**: you can merge the branch into `main` (or your integration branch) and delete the feature branch.

Example:
```bash
git checkout -b feature/scraper-progress-visibility
# ... do work ...
git add -A && git commit -m "Add scraper progress visibility when browser hidden"
```

Use descriptive branch names: `feature/...`, `fix/...`, `refactor/...`, `docs/...`.
